bio('timothy_mitchell','Timothy Mitchell investigates colonial power through the organization of space, knowledge and everyday administration. Colonising Egypt studies nineteenth-century arrangements that made populations and places appear ordered and governable. He connects disciplinary practices to colonial settings rather than treating them as developments confined to Europe. Rule of Experts and Carbon Democracy extend his historical inquiries into expertise, political economy and energy. His work combines historical research with political theory; the selected connections here rest on his own paperback preface to Colonising Egypt.',[event(1988,'Colonising Egypt',[mp],'Original1988 publication identified in institutional full-text citation; distinguished from1991 paperback.'),event(1991,'Colonising Egypt — paperback with new preface',[mp],'Read1991preface; later manifestation/new prefatory contribution, not a redated1988 original.',kind='edition',track='editions'),event(2002,'Rule of Experts: Egypt,Techno-Politics,Modernity',[mr],'UCPressNovember2002 original; full book unread.'),event(2011,'Carbon Democracy: Political Power in the Age of Oil',[mc],'Original2011 publication distinguished from2013 and2023 paperbacks; full book unread.')],[edge('post','Colonial power is examined through the production of ordered spaces and governable persons','Paperback preface ix–xi describes rural regulation, schooling and spatial partition; its historical claim concerns the power to colonise rather than a comprehensive narrative of British occupation.',[mp]),edge('spatialhistory','Spatial organization becomes part of an inquiry into governing power','Preface x–xii links surveillance, enclosure and exhibitionary order with colonial power, and locates disciplinary experiments beyond Europe. The connection concerns this documented analysis, not universal adoption by spatial historians.',[mp])],'Read1991paperback preface ix–xiii; bibliographic metadata supplies later dates only. No CarbonDemocracy or RuleofExperts argument is inferred from their titles.',[('post','Investigates colonial governing power through spatial and administrative arrangements.','Colonising Egypt(1988; paperbackpreface1991)',[mp],0)])
life('timothy_mitchell','living',[(ml,'Announcement22October2026','Positive institutional listing of an author book talk three days before check.')],limits='Evidence is current institutional author participation, not absence of a death record; an event listing does not independently establish delivery or survival after its date.')

