tb=source('todorov_bibliography','Société des Gens de Lettres, Tzvetan Todorov bibliography (1939–2017).','https://www.sgdl.org/phocadownload/actualit%C3%A9s_2017/Bibliographie_Tzvetan_Todorov.pdf','Read one-page professional-author bibliography entries1982,1991,1994; dates/credits only. Does not establish substantive argument. Later translated/revised manifestations distinct.',True)
th=source('todorov_translation','Smithsonian Libraries, The Conquest of America,Richard Howard translation; original English1984 note.','https://www.si.edu/object/siris_sil_897593','Indexed institutional title/translator and note “Originally published:NewYork:Harper&Row,c1984” checked. Current manifestation1999 is not the French1982original or firstEnglish1984. Body unread.',True)
tl=source('todorov_life','BnF authority cb11926748n,Tzvetan Todorov(1939–2017).','https://catalogue.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cb11926748n','Read authority fields:birth1March1939,Sofia;death7February2017,Paris; distinguishes CvetanTodorov1899–1962.',True)
bio('tzvetan_todorov','Tzvetan Todorov connected literary and semiotic inquiry with historical questions about conquest, moral choice and collective memory. La Conquête de l’Amérique uses the encounter between Europeans and Americans to examine relations with others; his short1984essay explicitly chooses Mexico as its historical case. Later works address extreme violence and wartime France. In his own essay on memory, commemoration does not automatically prevent renewed violence: narratives of past victimhood can also legitimate aggression. These selected arguments retain their ethical and interpretive character.',[event(1982,'La Conquête de l’Amérique:la question de l’autre',[tb],'FrenchSeuil1982original; RichardHoward Englishtranslation first1984, laterOklahoma1999edition distinguished.'),event(1984,'The Conquest of America — Richard Howard’s English translation',[th],'Harper&Row1984Englishpublication; not a new French original.',kind='edition',track='editions'),event(1991,'Face à l’extrême',[tb],'Seuil1991original; completebookunread.'),event(1994,'Une tragédie française,été1944:scènes de guerre civile',[tb],'Seuil1994original;2004revisededition not substituted for originaldate.')],[edge('post','Uses conquest as a historical case for examining attitudes toward other societies','The authored opening extract of “MoralityofConquest,”p89, explicitly identifies conquestofMexico and its texts as the case. This limited methodological connection does not assert the unread book’s full thesis or label Todorov a member of a later school.',[tq]),edge('memory','Challenges the assumption that remembering victimhood necessarily prevents violence','Own UNESCOessay distinguishes selective remembrance from ethical use and warns that former victims can become aggressors. This is his bounded intervention on public memory, not a psychological finding or a universal judgment on victims.',[tm])],'The colonial connection uses only three authored opening paragraphs of the1984essay; the memory connection uses his short UNESCOessay. Completehistoricalmonographs remain unread. Howard’stranslation and Frenchoriginal are distinguished;2018webpost is posthumous.',[('memory','Questions how selective public remembrance may serve either responsibility or renewed aggression.','“War:theevilthatmendo,”posthumousUNESCOwebreproduction',[tm],1)])
life('tzvetan_todorov','deceased',[(tl,'Authority birth/death and “do not confuse” fields','Exact birth1March1939 and death7February2017.')],1939,2017,'1939-03-01','2017-02-07',limits='National-library authority distinguishes the older Bulgarian namesake.')

