bio('alessandro_portelli','Alessandro Portelli examines oral testimony as an encounter that produces historical evidence. His studies of Italian workers and other communities distinguish the chronology of events from the meanings narrators give them. In his methodological essay, voice, rhythm and narrative form matter, while an interview’s questions and circumstances help shape its answers. Errors in a remembered date can therefore become evidence about memory without replacing the established event chronology. His work combines oral history with literature and music scholarship.',[event(1981,'The Peculiarities of Oral History',[pp],'HistoryWorkshop12,96–107;relatedItalian1979andEnglish1991versionsdistinguished. Thispacketreads adapted1991version, notexact1981transcription.'),event(1991,'The Death of Luigi Trastulli and Other Stories:Form and Meaning in Oral History',['portelli_stories',pp],'SUNY1991collection;componentessayshaveearlierhistories. Adaptedselected1991excerptread;wholecollectionunread.'),event(1997,'The Battle of Valle Giulia:Oral History and the Art of Dialogue',[pv],'WisconsinMay1997publication;fullbookunread.')],[edge('oral','Treats the interview as evidence produced through a relationship','Adapted1991excerpt,sectionIV, describes questions, changingrelationships and the distortion caused by removing the interviewer’s voice. The adaptationmodernizesbracketedterms; nottreatedasexact1981text.',[pp]),edge('memory','Uses displaced chronology to examine narrated meaning without changing event dates','Adaptedexcerpt,sectionIII, explicitly uses workers’ memoriesofTrastulli inTerni to distinguish whatoccurred from whatnarration means. Factualverification remains necessary; falsememoriesdo not replaceeventchronology.',[pp])],'Read allfourpages of the adapted1991excerpt “WhatMakesOralHistoryDifferent?”; sameboundedversion as earlierreview, with bracketedmodernizations. Original1979/1981texts andcompletebooksnotcollated.',[('memory','Studies the historical meaning of remembered narratives while retaining factual chronology.','Adapted1991“WhatMakesOralHistoryDifferent?”,sectionIII',[pp],1)],{pp:{'status':'supporting_page_checked','checked_on':DAY,'note':'Additional188review: reread complete4-pageadapted1991excerpt at existinghandoutURL. SectionsIII–IVsupport individualmemory/interviewrelationships.1979Italianoriginal,1981Englisharticleand1991relatedversionremaindistinct;handoutmodernizationsretainedasqualification;wholebooksunread.'}})
